  "owned_child": {
    "source": "coax/tests/systemone-fakecurl.c",
    "effects": "Reads exact two-byte stdin body; writes fixed JSON+200 or fixed stderr+exit28, or writes sleeping marker and sleeps until killed. No HTTP, sockets, environment keys, user files, model or network."
  },
  "checks": [
    "so_start with generated Coax default owner starts the owned child through actual process-native pipes; success returns borrowed body and usage, exit28 returns borrowed stderr.",
    "Success/exit28 child PID is already reaped: waitpid(WNOHANG) reports ECHILD and kill(pid,0) reports ESRCH.",
    "Copied success body/error descriptors preserve exact caller buffer pointer, extent and bytes after16KiB stack disturbance and duplicate terminal poll/cancel; surrounding guards remain intact.",
    "Sleeping child is observed through actual so_step nonblocking stdout handling, then so_cancel kills/reaps it.",
    "After every completion/cancel, native slot0 is reclaimable. Reserve that slot, issue duplicate cancel/poll on the retired owner, then a second native allocation returns slot1; retired operations did not release unrelated reusedslot0."
